//! Batch 354 — the sgl-muse-mega code-cache + cross-step-routing `kernel_opt`
//! distill (Plan 364 / Research 398): three CUDA-device-code mechanisms —
//! launch-time code-as-data L2 warming, the dry-pass instruction-cache warm,
//! and the previous-step-routing expert-weight prefetch — plus ONE
//! count-neutral rider face on its OWNER (`sentinel-readiness-over-separate-flag`
//! in `entries_gpu_30`).
//!
//! Source: `facebookresearch/sgl-muse-mega` @
//! `f009237dfc56ee130c1637352ff356093a870ecc` (main tip 2026-11-12, MIT ©
//! Meta; the `SGLang` megakernel lineage's second dedicated source — B333's
//! `sgl-project/sgl-nvidia-mega` is the first; every candidate below is
//! adjudicated against that landed set in-rule). Per the transcription law
//! the corpus consumes DECISION CONTENT with an ORIGINAL Rust fixture
//! (`corpus/fixtures/b354_fixtures.rs`, 3/3 standalone-compiled AND executed
//! before entry), never source verbatim — the CUDA surface is modeled as a
//! mock text/line layer; the fixture never calls a real GPU. Every quote
//! below byte-verified at the pin (T0 re-clone HEAD-equal; the layer.cu /
//! moe.cuh / `next_layer.cuh` / kernels/README.md line cites in-rule). The C+
//! self-stamping suggestion entry was DROPPED at authoring per the plan's
//! drop-allowed gate (no category slot — the `%globaltimer` DEADLINE axis is
